1pkg|v|A place where ships may ride secure from storms; a sheltered inlet, bay, or cove; a harbor; a haven. Used also figuratively. ; In law and commercial usage, a harbor where vessels are admitted to discharge and receive cargoes, from whence they depart and where they finish their voyages. ; To carry; to bear; to transport. ; To throw, as a musket, diagonally across the body, with the lock in front, the right hand grasping the small of the stock, and the barrel sloping upward and crossing the point of the left shoulder; as, to port arms. ; To turn or put to the left or larboard side of a ship; -- said of the helm, and used chiefly in the imperative, as a command; as, port your helm.	o:ixv,39,5;2bon,36,12~2bon,36,12;ixv,39,5	s:f8f,81,2;f5s,51,2;2bt5,44,1;27ts,43,2;rue,32,1;2dwb,4,5~2dwb,4,5;27ts,43,2;f5s,51,2;f8f,81,2;rue,32,1;2bt5,44,1	d:vn5,19,4~vn5,19,4	D:vn5,29,8~vn5,29,8
